                                        <table class="table table-bordered" width="80%" align="center" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                                            <tbody><tr>
                                                <td align="left" class="subheader class11">
                                                    Note on complexity levels of the rated instrument
                                                </td>
                                            </tr>
                                            <tr>
                                                <td>
                                                    <label class="normalfont class11">
                                                        <div style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'">­In order to inform the investors about complexity of instruments, Acuité has categorized such instruments in three levels: Simple, Complex and Highly Complex. Acuite’s categorisation of the instruments across the three categories is based on factors like variability of the returns to the investors, uncertainty in cash flow patterns, number of counterparties and general understanding of the instrument by the market. It has to be understood that complexity is different from credit risk and even an instrument categorized as 'Simple' can carry high levels of risk. For more details, please refer Rating Criteria “Complexity Level Of Financial Instruments” on&nbsp;<a href="https://www.acuite.in/view-rating-criteria-55.htm">www.acuite.in</a>.</span></div>

                                                    </label>
                                                </td>
                                            </tr>
                                        </tbody></table>
                                <table class="table table-bordered pgbrk" width="80%" align="center" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                                    <tbody><tr><td class="subheader class12"><br><label align="center" class="class9">Rating History</label></td></tr>

                                    <tr>
                                        <td>
                                            <table id="tbl_rath" class="table table-bordered" width="100%" align="center" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                                                <tbody><tr class="tbBrd">
                                                    <td class="subhead classtd1">Date</td>
                                                    <td class="subhead classtd2">Name of Instruments/Facilities</td>
                                                    <td class="subhead classtd2">Term</td>
                                                    <td class="subhead classtd2">Amount (Rs. Cr)</td>
                                                    <td class="subhead classtd2">Rating/Outlook</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                    <tr>
